  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759759,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## The Halley Project: A Mission In Our Solar System\n\nEmbark on an unprecedented scientific adventure in *The Halley Project*, a captivating space flight simulation for the Commodore 64. Assume the role of a skilled spacecraft pilot, hand-selected by the enigmatic organization P.L.A.N.E.T. to undertake *The Halley Project* – the ultimate challenge. Your mission: traverse the vast distances of our solar system, journeying from Halley's Comet to Earth and back again.\n\nProgress through challenging missions elevates your rank from Raven to Starbird, demanding precision and strategic planning. Realistic distances and planetary sizes contribute to a palpable sense of realism, requiring careful navigation and timing to achieve safe landings. A fictional hyperdrive allows for faster-than-light travel, while a sophisticated radar system aids in pinpointing planets and constellations. \n\nUnravel a secret mission accessible through a unique postcard-based code system, adding a layer of intrigue to the gameplay. Developed by Omar Khudari and Tom Snyder and published by Mindscape in 1985, *The Halley Project* seamlessly blends educational elements about our solar system with thrilling space exploration, offering a rewarding and immersive experience."
    },
